+and set `SLATE_SIGN_KEY=<private-key-hex>`.
 
-`sha256_chain` = SHA-256 of all included entry JSON payloads, concatenated in order. Verifying this hash confirms the bundle content was not modified after generation.
+## Verifying a bundle
 
-## Ed25519 signing
+A recipient needs the file and the public keys to trust, and nothing else:
 
 ```bash
-# Generate a key pair
-slate keygen
-# → prints public key (store in config) and private key (keep secret)
-
-# Export and sign
-export SLATE_SIGN_KEY=<private-key-hex>
-slate export --case CASE-2026-0042 --sign
+python3 tools/bundle-verify/verify_bundle.py bundle.ndjson \
+  --pin <export key> --pin <node key>
 ```
 
-The signature covers all bundle fields except the `signature` field itself (zeroed before signing). Verification:
+The verifier checks the pinned keys, the header signature, the entry count and
+digest, the head signature over `size ‖ root`, the case claim, and every inclusion
+proof. A v2 bundle cannot be assembled from entries that were never in the log:
+each proof ties the entry to the root the node signed.
 
-```go
-err := export.Verify(bundle, publicKeyHex)
-```
+## What the signature does and does not prove
+
+It proves the disclosed entries are leaves of the tree the node signed, and that
+the named export key signed this header. It does not prove the log was complete —
+the head is minted at export time from the log on this node — and it does not
+prove the timestamps, which are self-reported. Retaining a head outside the node
+at seal time is what would make the size and root independent of the node.
+
+`sha256_chain` is SHA-256 over the disclosed entry lines. It catches corruption;
+by itself it is not an authenticity claim, because it travels inside the document
+it describes.
+
+## Legacy v1 (`--format=1`)
+
+`slate export --case C --format=1` still writes the v1 bundle: the same NDJSON
+envelope, a single signature over the JSON encoding, and no inclusion proofs. Use
+it only for a counterpart that cannot check v2 yet. `--sign` still controls
+signing on that path.
 
