new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0915d86
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/bundle/testdata/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# `witness-bundle/2` test vectors
+
+These are the same frozen vectors as `tools/bundle-verify/testdata/` in
+mirror-node-reconnaissance, copied here so slate's own CI verifies the format
+rather than trusting a repository that is not in the loop.
+
+| File | Producer | Exercises |
+|---|---|---|
+| `v2-case.ndjson` | scratch Go emitter, §4 alone | `scope=case`, 4 of 500 entries, 9-hash audit paths |
+| `v2-log.ndjson` | scratch Go emitter, §4 alone | `scope=log`, all 12 entries, `entry_count == log_head.size` |
+| `v2-seven.ndjson` | scratch Go emitter, §4 alone | a 4+3 split whose right subtree splits again; 3-hash paths |
+| `v2-rust-log.ndjson` | `mnr bundle export` (Rust, `core/bundle`) | the same 12 entry lines as `v2-log.ndjson` |
+| `v2-rust-case.ndjson` | `mnr bundle export` (Rust, `core/bundle`) | 3 of 7 entries at seqs 2, 5, 7; indices 1, 4, 6 |
+| `v2-slate.ndjson` | `slate export` with this patch | 2 of 4 entries from a real store, distinct node and export keys |
+
+Each `*.export.pub` / `*.node.pub` is the public half of the key that signed the
+header or the tree head. A bundle is only ever checked against those pins, never
+against the key it names for itself — otherwise the document would vouch for its
+own signature.
+
+The private halves were throwaway and are gone; the records are fictional.
+
+Regenerate a fixture when the format changes. Do not hand-edit one: a fixture
+that no longer matches what a producer writes is a test that proves nothing.
